      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60e65f577ae9d0492b0f2a75|full_name} Well, for the people who use space dragging, it's a \"you know, you know\" — being an essential QoL feature provided by a 3rd-party plugin for the past 7–8+ years. Perhaps I expect too much here, but in my opinion VRChat not providing a similar feature natively after this amount of time seems like an oversight. Not calling them lazy devs, but they're complacent on it, probably because it has existed as OVRAS for as long as we know. While I want my QoL fixed, I'll admit I'm desperate to have somebody fix this problem because it sucks. I think all the Quest users who play standalone deserve this feature too, because they don't know what they're missing out on.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-11-15T20:08:50.244Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "There seems to be no hope of these plugins working anytime soon on the Steam Frame, such as OVRAS, with the resetting issues. It's had me thinking: VRChat would be awesome if they solved this problem by just adding native space dragging into the game, which would be more reliable than using some SteamVR addon anyway. Please seriously consider this — it would just be an overall upgrade, with one fewer SteamVR tool needed for any headset out there that has similar issues to the Frame's current ones.",
